  <!-- Deterministic, IP-independent SEO city landing pages —
       /events/{city-slug}/ (routes/cityPage.js, data/seo-cities.js).
       Scaled from the original 3-city pilot (Berlin, Essen, Dresden —
       spec section 35's own staged-rollout instruction) to all 12
       German cities already established elsewhere on the site (same
       list as data/major-cities.js's DE entry), after the pilot was
       independently verified live. These are DIFFERENT from
       /cities/germany/ above — that page (and /api/cities generally)
       is IP/country-driven, correct for the interactive browse
       experience but explicitly NOT meant to be what determines
       indexability. Every one of these always renders the same city
       regardless of who/what requests them.

       Each city also has a /concerts/ sub-page — same city record,
       same SSR architecture, filtered to Ticketmaster's real Music
       segment only (routes/cityPage.js's renderCityConcertsPage).
       Deliberately a separate URL/canonical from the general page
       above, not a query-string filter, per the explicit instruction
       that search/filter URLs must never be the canonical SEO page.

       Only page 1 of each is listed here — deeper pagination pages
       (/page/2/, etc.) are real and indexable but discovered via
       rel=next/prev and internal pagination links rather than being
       enumerated in the static sitemap, consistent with standard
       practice for paginated listings. -->
